/* book Worked example: Q: A six-speed spindle has nmin = 100 rpm and φ = 1.41. Find all six speeds, the maximum speed and the speed range.
   1. n1 = 100 rpm; n2 = 100 × 1.41 = 141 rpm.
   2. n3 = 100 × 1.41² = 100 × 1.9881 = 198.8 rpm; n4 = 100 × 1.41³ = 280.3 rpm.
   3. n5 = 100 × 1.41⁴ = 100 × 3.9525 = 395.3 rpm; n6 = 100 × 1.41⁵ = 557.3 rpm.
   4. Rounded to the standard series: 100, 140, 200, 280, 400, 560 rpm.
   5. Range: Rn = 557.3/100 = 5.57 (5.6 with the standard speeds), which is φ⁵.
   Answer: 100, 141, 198.8, 280.3, 395.3 and 557.3 rpm (standard 100, 140, 200, 280, 400, 560); maximum 557 rpm; range 5.57. */
